cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Research Assistant Scaffold
message: >-
  If you use this kit, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Bernard
    family-names: Slippers
    affiliation: >-
      Forestry and Agricultural Biotechnology Institute (FABI),
      University of Pretoria, South Africa
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # uncomment and add yours
repository-code: 'https://github.com/FABI-UP/research-assistant-scaffold'
abstract: >-
  A domain-agnostic scaffold and agent skill for working with an agentic,
  file-aware AI research assistant across many sessions, machines and projects.
  Ships two profiles: a repository profile for work that runs, with a state
  model, step contract, configuration layer and verification tooling; and a
  library profile for work that accumulates, with a naming convention, an index
  ledger, intake discipline and a checker that recounts a collection from the
  filesystem. Contains no domain-specific science.
keywords:
  - research software engineering
  - AI agents
  - reproducibility
  - research data management
  - open science
